This problem of combining hypothesis test rejection P-values is hardly a new one; and there is an extensive, long-established, and still-active literature, beginning with Fisher (5), addressing this topic.
Most of this literature is concerned with the ‘Big Data’ problem of combining a large number of P-values. One of these methods – notably the “HMP P-value Combination Method” put forth by Wilson (8) is very promising in this context, and may well represent a future path for the topic at hand. But, for the present work, the most relevant and effective approach remains the same ‘Fisher’s Combined Probability Test’ – based on the seminal Fisher (1925) paper – which we applied in Ashley and Patterson (1).
